<!-- Section 1: Overview & The Nine Defining Dimensions -->
<section class="mb-16 lg:mb-24 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-4  lg:gap-8 items-start">
    
    <!-- Left Column: Narrative Content & Dimensions -->
    <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-8 text-balance">
      
      <!-- Introductory Lead -->
      <div class="space-y-4 ">
        <p>
          The ongoing digitalisation of sport is giving rise to new sporting formats and disciplines (for example, the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.uci.org/discipline/cycling-esports/5awP766tEGOobRlwSdHBDs?discipline=CES">UCI's cycling esports</a>) that blur the boundaries between traditional sports and video gaming. 
          Rather than treating these formats as mere games or temporary trends, this page outlines why it makes sense to recognise and understand them as new distinct sporting disciplines that are here to stay.
          In what follows, we discuss what virtual sports are, why they matter, whom they impact, and how their future is taking shape.
        </p>
        <p>
          To make sense of virtual sports as emerging digitlised sporting disciplines, we link back to foundational concepts developed in social sciences and sport management.
          Most of the items explained on this page have been developed as part of <a href="/members/thibault-fouquaert">Thibault Fouquaert's</a> doctoral dissertation (Ghent University, Belgium) on the topic of virtual sports.
          For those who want to read or explore a more comprehensive and scientific analysis of virtual sports and some of the concepts discussed below, can consult the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://biblio.ugent.be/publication/01KWESKD8T405VTFE3PADRE2JB">full open access text (UGent Biblio)</a> of Thibault's disseration online.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 1 Header -->
      <div class="pt-4 border-t border-slate-200/80">
        <!-- <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase bg-vs-yellow-100 text-vs-yellow-900 border border-vs-yellow-300/80 mb-3">
          <span>Framework</span>
          <span class="w-1 h-1 rounded-full bg-vs-yellow-600"></span>
          <span>Part 1</span>
