        <h3 class="md:text-2xl text-3xl font-bold text-vs-blue-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">
          What Virtual Sports Are: Defining Dimensions
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          To identify what sets virtual sports apart, we can look at sport activities across nine universal dimensions of traditional sports. 
          These dimensions, originally developed in sport sociology literature (e.g. Guttmann, 2004; Loy, 1968), provide a structure to compare virtual sports against esports, exergames. 
          While such a structure helps in comparing distinct aspect of these activities, they are not compared to develop an order of which activity is "better". 
          Rather, it makes it possible to specifiy and categorise differences.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- The Nine Dimensions List -->
      <ol class="space-y-4 lg:space-y-6 leading-relaxed" role="list">
        
        <!-- Dimension 1 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            1
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Human Agency:</strong>
            The outcome is driven by real human capability, decision-making, and exertion, rather than automated scripts or artificial intelligence.
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- Dimension 2 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            2
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Voluntary Participation:</strong>
            Engagement is non-coercive and motivated by personal enjoyment, health, community belonging, or competitive ambition.
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- Dimension 3 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            3
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Competition:</strong>
            Contests range from friendly community group rides to formal national championships and global events like the Olympic Esports Series or the UCI Cycling Esports World Championships.
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- Dimension 4 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            4
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Physicality:</strong>
            Requires gross-motor, athletic movement that actively mimics the biomechanics of an existing parent sport.
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- Dimension 5 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            5
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Cognitivity:</strong>
            Demands real-time strategic thinking, tactical pacing, and situational awareness.
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- Dimension 6 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            6
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Following:</strong>
            Supported by a dedicated, growing community transitioning from active participants into digital spectators.
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- Dimension 7 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            7
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Governance:</strong>
            Governed through a dual structure involving traditional sports governing bodies (e.g., UCI, World Triathlon) alongside commercial software platform providers.
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- Dimension 8 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            8
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Institutionalisation:</strong>
            Regulated by official competition rulebooks, structured calendar leagues, anti-doping policies, and recognized federation disciplines.
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- Dimension 9 -->
        <li class="flex items-start gap-4 ">
          <span class="flex-none flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-vs-blue-900 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-xs">
            9
          </span>
          <div class="text-base md:text-lg">
            <strong class="font-bold text-vs-blue-900 block sm:inline sm:mr-1">Reality:</strong>
            Competitions take place within a distinct physical-digital interreality where physical effort is translated and altered by virtual-world algorithms and physics engines.
          </div>
        </li>

      </ol>

    </div>

